      "description": "Home identity, controller context, and the settings disclosure.",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-masthead\"><a class=\"ds-wordmark\" href=\"#home\"><span class=\"ds-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Note calendar</a><span class=\"ds-host\">Your Raspberry Pi controller</span><button class=\"ds-settings\" aria-expanded=\"false\">Settings</button></header>",
      "css": ".ds-masthead{height:86px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:24px;max-width:1328px;padding:0 36px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule,#d9d9ce);font-family:\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-wordmark{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;color:var(--ink,#292b28);text-decoration:none;font-size:19px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.03em}.ds-mark{width:22px;height:26px;background:linear-gradient(to right,var(--red,#871f2b) 0 7px,var(--white,#fffef9) 7px);border:1px solid var(--red,#871f2b);border-radius:3px}.ds-host{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted,#63665f);margin-left:auto}.ds-settings{background:none;border:0;color:var(--ink,#292b28);font:600 13px/1.55 \"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif;min-height:40px;padding:8px 0 8px 12px;cursor:pointer}.ds-settings:hover{color:var(--red,#871f2b)}.ds-settings:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#995d13);outline-offset:4px}.ds-wordmark:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--focus,#995d13);outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:760px){.ds-masthead{padding:0 22px;height:72px;gap:12px}.ds-host{display:none}.ds-settings{margin-left:auto}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The supplied desk calendar",
    "overview": "The user's original photograph is the visual authority: a warm paper field, a deep red sidebar, compact proportional sans-serif lettering, a small week strip, and a holiday illustration. This document records the implemented system in render.py, typography.py, art.py, index.html, and app.css. It does not establish a separate generated comp or direction seed.\n\nThe Note output is a dense, glanceable pixel composition. The browser companion supports inspecting that output, reading displayed events, connecting a calendar, and managing the device. Its quiet system typography and restrained controls keep attention on the calendar preview.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A fixed four-color native frame with a strong red date-and-holiday sidebar.",
      "Native proportional sans-serif lettering, single-line events, and date groups that consume available height.",
      "Original geometric holiday sprites with deliberately visible pixel edges.",
      "A warm, responsive browser workspace with an accessible text equivalent of the preview."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Reference Rule",
        "body": "Preserve the supplied photograph's compact visual language while honoring the user's explicit content changes.",
        "section": "overview"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Four Inks Rule",
        "body": "Native pixels use only palette indices 0 through 3: black, white, yellow, and red. The frame is an indexed image, not an antialiased RGB illustration. The native-color PNG option substitutes pure device colors; the binary frame preserves those same index meanings.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Native Pixels Rule",
        "body": "Preserve glyph edges with integer pixel drawing and nearest-neighbor enlargement. Keep event titles on one line. The renderer fits long text to the available width with three periods and normalizes unsupported characters.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Available Height Rule",
        "body": "Fill the agenda according to the space occupied by real date groups and rows. Do not reserve blank weeks or assume a fixed event count.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Device Surround Rule",
        "body": "Use the existing preview shell's shadows to distinguish the displayed object from its page. Do not add those shadows to agenda groups or control sections.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the original photograph's red sidebar, paper agenda, proportional sans-serif lettering, and small holiday illustration.",
      "Do render the Note frame at 400 by 300 indexed pixels and use nearest-neighbor enlargement.",
      "Do use day and date, single-line events, 12-hour times, and a rounded red badge only for today.",
      "Do let event capacity follow the actual date groups and available height.",
      "Do keep one holiday in the sidebar, with its date independent from its artwork.",
      "Do keep browser source state explicit and pair the preview with readable event text.",
      "Do preserve visible focus, labeled controls, and reduced-motion behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put week numbers, a calendar name, an account email, or a \"Next holiday\" label on the Note screen.",
      "Don't antialias native text, blur enlarged pixels, or introduce colors outside the four native indices.",
      "Don't turn the busy fixture's 12 displayed events into a fixed product capacity.",
      "Don't stretch the native frame or reflow its agenda at browser breakpoints.",
      "Don't treat a screenshot or documentation label as a new approved visual comp.",
      "Don't use em dashes in product copy or project documentation."
    ]
  }
}
